import ../../../testing/driver.dl

set submissions to 0
function [record a culled shape] {a pointer to UI view:view} vertices {a pointer to UI vertex:vertices} counting {integer:count} with {a pointer:texture}:
    globals:
        submissions
    execute:
        require condition (count > 0) reporting "A shape submitted empty geometry"
        increment submissions

document shape fixture:
    paragraph "Fixture" using no UI appearance
set instance to an instance of shape fixture
set driver to the value at (the test UI driver)
set driver's triangles to (the function named "record a culled shape $ vertices $ counting $ with $") as a pointer
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 100 by 100 using font "regular" with (the address of driver)
set view's clip to UI box at 0.0 0.0 sized 100.0 100.0
set frame to @intrinsic("construct", UI frame, the address of view, true)
set ink to UI ink 255 255 255
draw a rounded UI box (UI box at 10.0 150.0 sized 20.0 20.0) with radius 4.0 in ink on frame
draw a rounded UI outline (UI box at 10.0 150.0 sized 20.0 20.0) with radius 4.0 width 2.0 in ink on frame
require condition (submissions = 0) reporting "Clipped shapes still built and submitted geometry"
draw a rounded UI surface (UI box at 10.0 110.0 sized 20.0 20.0) with radius 4.0 from ink to ink opacity 120 feathered by 12.0 on frame
require condition (submissions = 1) reporting "Culling discarded a visible shadow fringe"
move the model in frame by x 200.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
rotate the model in frame by 90.0 degrees around x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0
draw a rounded UI box (UI box at 10.0 150.0 sized 20.0 20.0) with radius 4.0 in ink on frame
require condition (submissions = 2) reporting "Culling ignored the model transform"
set view's transform to the identity UI transform
move the model in frame by x -200.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
draw a rounded UI box (UI box at 10.0 10.0 sized 20.0 20.0) with radius 4.0 in ink on frame
require condition (submissions = 2) reporting "A transformed shape outside the clip still submitted geometry"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Shape culling respects transforms, clipping and visible antialiasing fringes."
